  "scenario": "A defense contractor needs to secure its communications with the Department of Defense (DoD). The contractor uses a VPN with IKEv2/IPsec, with RSA-2048 and DH Group 14. The DoD has mandated that all VPN traffic must use 'quantum-safe' cryptography by 2027. A vendor offers a 'quantum-safe VPN' appliance that uses pre-shared keys (PSK) with 256-bit entropy, claiming it is 'quantum-safe' because PSK is not vulnerable to Shor's algorithm. The contractor has a budget of $400,000 and a change freeze from Dec 1 to Jan 15. The contractor's network team has no PQC experience. The DoD has specified that they will only accept NIST-standardized PQC algorithms (ML-KEM, ML-DSA). The vendor's appliance does not support ML-KEM or ML-DSA.",
